@startuml
title Native session transport
hide footbox
participant "Mobile auth controller" as Client
database "Secure OS storage" as Store
participant "Mobile API controller" as API
participant "Existing auth handler" as Handler
database "SQL Server" as DB
Client -> API : POST /api/auth/mobile/login\nemail + password
API -> Handler : LoginCommand + request metadata
Handler -> DB : Save refresh token hash + family
Handler --> API : Token pair + expiry
API --> Client : JSON; no-store; no cookie
Client -> Store : Persist refresh token
note over Client : Access token stays in memory
Client -> Store : Read refresh token on restart / expiry
Store --> Client : Refresh token
Client -> API : POST /api/auth/mobile/refresh\nrefreshToken JSON
API -> Handler : RefreshTokenCommand
Handler -> DB : Validate; revoke old token; save replacement
Handler --> API : Rotated token pair
API --> Client : JSON; no-store
Client -> Store : Replace refresh token before publishing session
Client -> Store : Read latest refresh token for logout
Store --> Client : Captured credential
Client -> Store : Delete local credential; clear in-memory session
Client -> API : POST /api/auth/mobile/sign-out\nrefreshToken JSON
API -> Handler : SignOutCommand
Handler -> DB : Revoke presented token if active
API --> Client : 204
@enduml
